WEBVTT

00:00:01.330 --> 00:00:03.020
You look stunning!

00:00:03.520 --> 00:00:05.520
Yume-chan, you're gorgeous!

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:08.330
A walking firework blooming 
before our very eyes!

00:00:08.330 --> 00:00:10.970
This year's show is gonna be a total flop!

00:00:10.970 --> 00:00:13.780
Er, that's enough, Madoka-san.

00:00:14.090 --> 00:00:15.390
Why, you ask?

00:00:15.390 --> 00:00:17.280
Because everyone's eyes will be on <i>you</i>!

00:00:18.040 --> 00:00:19.790
Are you making fun of me?

00:00:20.400 --> 00:00:23.080
Nonsense! I'm speaking from the heart.

00:00:23.080 --> 00:00:25.230
Doesn't she look cute, Chikuma?

00:00:25.230 --> 00:00:26.010
Yeah...

00:00:26.720 --> 00:00:28.540
Oh, Mizuto-kun's here.

00:00:36.120 --> 00:00:37.950
Well? Whaddya think, Mizuto-kun?

00:00:37.950 --> 00:00:39.680
Isn't she beautiful?

00:00:41.660 --> 00:00:42.810
C-Can...

00:00:43.090 --> 00:00:43.810
Hmm?

00:00:43.810 --> 00:00:46.560
Can I... Can I get a picture?!

00:00:46.920 --> 00:00:48.060
Huh?

00:00:48.060 --> 00:00:50.060
Okay! One picture coming right up!

00:00:50.060 --> 00:00:50.690
Huh?

00:00:51.020 --> 00:00:53.150
Make sure to get a good angle, Mizuto-kun.

00:00:53.150 --> 00:00:55.200
Er, no... I didn't mean of me.

00:00:56.450 --> 00:00:57.820
<b>Enter Password</b>

00:00:57.820 --> 00:00:58.820
Huh?

00:01:00.330 --> 00:01:03.700
H-How did you know my password?!

00:01:14.340 --> 00:01:16.380
<b>My Stepmom's 
Daughter Is 
My Ex</b>

00:02:36.130 --> 00:02:41.510
<b>I Bestow Unto You My First Kiss</b>

00:02:38.050 --> 00:02:39.960
What made you come with us?

00:02:40.520 --> 00:02:43.270
Don't you hate big crowds like this?

00:02:43.720 --> 00:02:45.670
Madoka doesn't have anyone else, you know?

00:02:46.190 --> 00:02:50.190
She makes a point of dragging 
me here every year.

00:02:50.820 --> 00:02:54.440
I've given up trying to resist at this point.

00:02:55.940 --> 00:02:59.570
I could ask you the same. 
Don't you hate big crowds too?

00:03:01.190 --> 00:03:04.200
I suppose I don't have good memories of them.

00:03:04.580 --> 00:03:06.190
We're back!

00:03:06.190 --> 00:03:08.830
The restrooms were packed, 
so it took us a bit.

00:03:09.260 --> 00:03:11.640
Why don't you two hold hands too?

00:03:11.640 --> 00:03:13.460
That way, you won't get separated.

00:03:13.800 --> 00:03:15.960
We're not children.

00:03:15.960 --> 00:03:18.710
Besides, even if we did get separated,
 I'd just head back home—

00:03:21.720 --> 00:03:23.090
What are you doing?

00:03:23.420 --> 00:03:26.080
This is normal between siblings.

00:03:26.080 --> 00:03:27.180
Huh?

00:03:27.180 --> 00:03:30.350
It's my responsibility as your
 older sister to keep you close.

00:03:30.670 --> 00:03:32.060
Exactly!

00:03:32.060 --> 00:03:33.980
Couldn't have said
 it better myself, Yume-chan!

00:03:33.980 --> 00:03:36.120
Have you forgotten?

00:03:36.120 --> 00:03:37.480
I'm the older brother, remember?

00:03:37.800 --> 00:03:41.110
Fine by me. Doesn't matter either way.

00:03:41.520 --> 00:03:45.280
All the same, it's your responsibility 
as the older brother to keep her close.

00:03:47.280 --> 00:03:48.750
Fine.

00:03:48.750 --> 00:03:50.600
All I have to do is hold your hand, right?

00:03:50.600 --> 00:03:53.020
Look at you, doing as you're told.

00:03:53.020 --> 00:03:54.120
Shut up.

00:03:55.120 --> 00:03:59.320
<i>I feel so much lighter after 
crying my eyes out yesterday.</i>

00:04:00.340 --> 00:04:04.130
<i>It's like I finally let go of all the
 needless baggage I was carrying around.</i>

00:04:06.540 --> 00:04:09.140
Is there anything you guys want to eat?

00:04:09.760 --> 00:04:14.650
Granny gave us plenty of spending money,
 so feel free to go wild, okay?

00:04:14.650 --> 00:04:17.530
Festival stalls are always
 so expensive, though.

00:04:17.960 --> 00:04:20.820
I feel like we should just go 
to the convenience store.

00:04:20.820 --> 00:04:22.730
Don't get your hopes up.

00:04:22.730 --> 00:04:25.320
We're in the countryside. 
You're not gonna find one around here.

00:04:26.950 --> 00:04:29.370
<b>Shooting Gallery</b>

00:04:26.950 --> 00:04:29.370
Bull's-eye!!

00:04:27.480 --> 00:04:29.370
Oh, look! They have a shooting game!

00:04:29.710 --> 00:04:30.920
Wanna try, Chikuma?

00:04:30.920 --> 00:04:32.500
Y-Yeah.

00:04:33.240 --> 00:04:34.250
All right!

00:04:34.250 --> 00:04:36.880
<b>Y o - k a i   Q u e s t</b>

00:04:34.250 --> 00:04:36.880
<b>Yo-kai Quest</b>

00:04:34.590 --> 00:04:36.880
Let's aim for the big prize
 together, you and me!

00:04:42.200 --> 00:04:43.630
Maybe a little more to the right.

00:04:43.630 --> 00:04:48.260
<i>D-Do siblings normally
 get that close to each other?</i>

00:04:44.660 --> 00:04:46.340
That's too much, too much!

00:04:48.260 --> 00:04:51.440
All right, Chikuma, hold it steady...

00:04:51.440 --> 00:04:52.390
Here goes!

00:04:52.390 --> 00:04:53.270
<b>Y o - k a i   Q u e s t</b>

00:04:52.390 --> 00:04:53.270
<b>Yo-kai Quest</b>

00:04:53.270 --> 00:04:54.140
<b>Yo-kai Quest</b>

00:04:54.140 --> 00:04:55.600
<b>Yo-kai Quest</b>

00:04:54.140 --> 00:04:55.600
<b>Y o - k a i   Q u e s t</b>

00:04:54.880 --> 00:04:56.780
Aw, too bad.

00:04:56.780 --> 00:04:57.820
Yeah...

00:04:58.360 --> 00:05:01.610
<b>Shooting Gallery</b>

00:04:58.360 --> 00:05:01.610
Bull's-eye!!

00:04:59.580 --> 00:05:01.610
We can't let it end like this.

00:05:01.930 --> 00:05:03.610
You're up, Mizuto-kun!

00:05:03.920 --> 00:05:05.740
Avenge Chikuma, would you?

00:05:06.210 --> 00:05:08.120
All right, one shot and that's it.

00:05:10.990 --> 00:05:13.320
Go help him, Yume-chan.

00:05:13.320 --> 00:05:14.780
As his big sister.

00:05:14.780 --> 00:05:16.320
What? Um, but...

00:05:16.320 --> 00:05:17.280
What's this now?

00:05:17.280 --> 00:05:21.880
You'd just be holding your 
little brother from behind.

00:05:21.880 --> 00:05:24.760
What could you possibly be flustered about?

00:05:29.260 --> 00:05:30.160
Hey...

00:05:30.160 --> 00:05:33.910
H-Hey! Quit looking at me 
and focus on aiming!

00:05:35.180 --> 00:05:36.920
Aren't you a little off to the right?

00:05:36.920 --> 00:05:38.640
No, I'm not.

00:05:38.640 --> 00:05:39.950
Yes, you are!

00:05:39.950 --> 00:05:42.190
Quit nagging me. Is this better?

00:05:42.190 --> 00:05:44.030
You're too far left!

00:05:44.030 --> 00:05:47.070
More to the right.
Yeah, just a little more...

00:05:47.920 --> 00:05:49.710
<i>Th-This is bad...</i>

00:05:49.710 --> 00:05:51.580
<i>I don't think my legs can 
hold out much longer.</i>

00:05:51.870 --> 00:05:54.580
<i>A-At this rate, my chest is gonna...</i>

00:05:55.190 --> 00:05:56.080
This is it.

00:06:06.400 --> 00:06:08.000
Doesn't suit you one bit.

00:06:08.000 --> 00:06:11.600
Have you no concept of the
 phrase "keep it to yourself"?

00:06:12.050 --> 00:06:12.820
Here.

00:06:17.680 --> 00:06:19.500
Th-Thanks.

00:06:19.500 --> 00:06:21.360
Wasn't that nice of him, Chikuma?

00:06:21.820 --> 00:06:24.610
How did you know he wanted it?

00:06:24.920 --> 00:06:28.990
It's a character from the game 
he's been playing recently.

00:06:29.280 --> 00:06:32.410
Really? I'm surprised you 
noticed something like that.

00:06:35.620 --> 00:06:39.080
To think you're this socially 
awkward with kids too.

00:06:39.080 --> 00:06:40.520
What do you mean "too"?

00:06:40.520 --> 00:06:43.080
When have I ever been socially awkward?

00:06:43.080 --> 00:06:47.470
I'm starting to feel resistance to the idea 
of letting you be the older brother.

00:06:47.470 --> 00:06:50.380
Better that than letting you
 be the older sister.

00:06:51.020 --> 00:06:53.390
Speaking of, did you do
 that on purpose earlier?

00:06:55.550 --> 00:06:57.600
N-Never in a million years!

00:06:57.980 --> 00:06:59.180
That's a relief.

00:06:59.180 --> 00:07:02.230
I'm glad my stepsister 
isn't a complete pervert.

00:07:02.230 --> 00:07:03.070
Perv—?!

00:07:03.070 --> 00:07:06.330
Wh-What's got you so hot
 and bothered about it anyway?

00:07:06.330 --> 00:07:08.860
I thought you'd be used to it
 after hanging out with Higashira-san.

00:07:09.400 --> 00:07:12.990
She comes at me without a second thought,

00:07:12.990 --> 00:07:15.950
but when you do it, 
I can tell you're nervous.

00:07:15.950 --> 00:07:17.370
Try to relax for once.

00:07:17.370 --> 00:07:18.250
Wha—

00:07:18.250 --> 00:07:22.760
Y-You're making it sound like
 Higashira-san's better with boys than I am!

00:07:22.760 --> 00:07:24.170
Okay, okay!

00:07:24.880 --> 00:07:26.870
Time to get a move on, you two!

00:07:30.520 --> 00:07:33.240
Oh, look over there!
 It's Uncle Mineaki and Aunt Yuni.

00:07:33.240 --> 00:07:35.140
Who are they talking to?

00:07:35.140 --> 00:07:36.730
What was her name again?

00:07:36.730 --> 00:07:40.840
We used to be pretty big in
 town back in the day, you see.

00:07:40.840 --> 00:07:43.150
So lots of older folks 
around here know the family.

00:07:43.150 --> 00:07:46.270
Yume! Mizuto-kun!

00:07:48.280 --> 00:07:50.030
Perfect timing.

00:07:50.030 --> 00:07:52.170
Kedouin-san, this is my daughter.

00:07:52.170 --> 00:07:53.910
I'm Irido Yume.

00:07:53.910 --> 00:07:57.530
My goodness. What a pretty young lady you are.

00:07:57.840 --> 00:08:01.540
I see Mizuto-kun finally has someone 
to call family other than his father.

00:08:02.160 --> 00:08:05.550
When I heard what happened from Natsume,
 I was worried sick.

00:08:05.550 --> 00:08:08.970
I'm sure you have your hands full 
getting used to your new lives,

00:08:08.970 --> 00:08:11.800
but do remember to look after Mizuto-kun.

00:08:12.480 --> 00:08:13.300
Of course.

00:08:14.240 --> 00:08:15.260
<i>How strange...</i>

00:08:16.040 --> 00:08:21.310
<i>She makes it sound as if he can't survive 
without someone there to watch over him.</i>

00:08:21.310 --> 00:08:26.720
We've reserved the perfect viewing
 spot for the fireworks for you all.

00:08:26.720 --> 00:08:28.320
I can take you there, if you'd like.

00:08:28.320 --> 00:08:30.970
Thank you as always.

00:08:30.970 --> 00:08:33.240
The fireworks show starts at eight, right?

00:08:33.240 --> 00:08:34.280
Yeah.

00:08:34.280 --> 00:08:36.810
We still have some time before the fireworks.

00:08:36.810 --> 00:08:38.090
What would you all like to do?

00:08:38.090 --> 00:08:40.200
Oh? Where'd Mizuto-kun go?

00:08:40.540 --> 00:08:41.190
What?

00:08:42.090 --> 00:08:44.830
Uh-oh, he's run off on his own again, has he?

00:08:45.210 --> 00:08:50.460
Mizuto-kun always disappears
 right before the fireworks every year.

00:08:52.340 --> 00:08:54.960
<i>I see... That explains it.</i>

00:08:56.260 --> 00:08:57.720
<i>I get it now.</i>

00:08:58.200 --> 00:09:01.880
<i>Mizuto was probably 
uncomfortable in that setting.</i>

00:09:01.880 --> 00:09:02.810
<i>So that's why...</i>

00:09:03.120 --> 00:09:04.810
Sure. Thanks, kid.

00:09:05.080 --> 00:09:09.070
<i>His dad must have been thanking him
 for coming along anyway.</i>

00:09:09.070 --> 00:09:13.530
<i>But it's not that Mizuto
 is uninterested in his relatives.</i>

00:09:14.460 --> 00:09:16.320
<i>If he were completely indifferent to them,</i>

00:09:16.850 --> 00:09:21.200
<i>he never would've thought 
to give Chikuma that toy.</i>

00:09:21.760 --> 00:09:24.830
I'm sorry, but I can't go out with you.

00:09:25.160 --> 00:09:27.570
I'm selfish.

00:09:27.570 --> 00:09:31.210
I can't be attentive to more 
than one person at a time.

00:09:31.550 --> 00:09:33.920
And the one slot that I have...

00:09:33.920 --> 00:09:38.220
It's already occupied by someone else, 
even though she doesn't deserve it.

00:09:40.480 --> 00:09:43.050
It must be pretty windy out, huh?

00:09:43.050 --> 00:09:45.230
<i>Oh... Yeah.</i>

00:09:46.520 --> 00:09:47.530
<i>Ayai?</i>

00:09:47.530 --> 00:09:48.550
Hmm?

00:09:48.550 --> 00:09:49.480
<i>Never mind.</i>

00:09:51.010 --> 00:09:54.360
<i>Actually, my battery's getting pretty low.</i>

00:09:55.520 --> 00:09:59.100
<i>Why couldn't we talk
while his phone was charging?</i>

00:10:00.570 --> 00:10:02.580
August 22nd (Sat)

00:10:03.350 --> 00:10:04.580
<i>That wasn't it.</i>

00:10:04.950 --> 00:10:07.460
August 12th (Sat)

00:10:08.340 --> 00:10:10.170
<i>I didn't know.</i>

00:10:10.720 --> 00:10:12.840
<i>The person I was two years ago didn't know...</i>

00:10:13.730 --> 00:10:16.490
<i>that he'd be visiting his 
relatives this time of year</i>

00:10:16.490 --> 00:10:20.840
<i>and trailing around the local festival.</i>

00:10:22.040 --> 00:10:23.930
<i>When we were just classmates...</i>

00:10:25.060 --> 00:10:26.430
<i>When I was his girlfriend...</i>

00:10:27.300 --> 00:10:30.440
<i>And ever since we became family...</i>

00:10:31.190 --> 00:10:33.070
<i>I've gotten to see many facets of Irido Mizuto.</i>

00:10:34.940 --> 00:10:38.320
<i>They fit together like puzzle pieces,
 one after another,</i>

00:10:40.570 --> 00:10:43.130
<i>forming a three-dimensional image of him.</i>

00:10:43.600 --> 00:10:45.500
<i>One I never knew.</i>

00:10:45.500 --> 00:10:49.390
<i>A picture of him I never would have seen
if I'd stayed just his girlfriend.</i>

00:10:49.390 --> 00:10:50.170
<i>But still...</i>

00:10:51.270 --> 00:10:52.830
I'm going to go find him.

00:10:53.640 --> 00:10:55.340
Yeah, go get him.

00:10:59.420 --> 00:11:02.390
<b>The Siberian Dancing Girl</b>

00:11:05.260 --> 00:11:09.020
I wanted you to stop me from leaving.

00:11:05.610 --> 00:11:09.700
"I wanted you to stop me from leaving."

00:11:11.020 --> 00:11:13.020
<b>My Stepmom's Daughter Is My Ex</b>

00:11:20.780 --> 00:11:24.400
<i>For as long as I can remember, 
nothing's ever felt real to me.</i>

00:11:25.700 --> 00:11:27.780
<i>Like I was living someone else's life.</i>

00:11:28.200 --> 00:11:30.290
<i>Like I was living in a fictional world.</i>

00:11:31.030 --> 00:11:34.540
<i>Everything about the 
"wonders of life" people speak of</i>

00:11:34.540 --> 00:11:37.550
<i>seemed like a faraway fantasy
that only existed in my TV.</i>

00:11:38.280 --> 00:11:41.550
<i>And I wasn't just pretending 
to be the guy from </i>No Longer Human<i>.</i>

00:11:41.550 --> 00:11:44.550
<i>I genuinely couldn't identify with anyone.</i>

00:11:44.550 --> 00:11:47.870
It's a miracle you were born safe and sound.

00:11:47.870 --> 00:11:50.560
It must be so hard growing up
 without a mother.

00:11:50.940 --> 00:11:55.560
<i>I never understood why
 they pitied and praised me</i>

00:11:56.090 --> 00:12:00.320
<i>for simply existing, 
for simply breathing the air around me.</i>

00:12:00.320 --> 00:12:02.570
<i>I didn't get it. I didn't understand.</i>

00:12:03.380 --> 00:12:07.850
<i>And because of that,
 a hole begun to grow within me...</i>

00:12:08.580 --> 00:12:11.930
<i>until everything passed right through 
me without so much as a sound.</i>

00:12:12.330 --> 00:12:15.960
<i>But despite that, the one and only 
thing that ever felt real to me</i>

00:12:15.960 --> 00:12:18.210
<b>The Siberian Dancing Girl</b>

00:12:16.440 --> 00:12:18.210
<i>was the world of the written word.</i>

00:12:18.920 --> 00:12:20.480
<i>I will never forget the impact</i>

00:12:20.480 --> 00:12:23.960
<i>of reading my great-grandfather's 
"The Siberian Dancing Girl"</i>

00:12:23.960 --> 00:12:25.720
<i>for the very first time.</i>

00:12:26.450 --> 00:12:30.510
<i>My soul glimpsed the world 
as reflected in its pages.</i>

00:12:30.510 --> 00:12:32.070
<i>And for once, I felt connected to it.</i>

00:12:32.480 --> 00:12:35.480
<b>The Dancing Girl 
 Foam on the Waves
 And three other tales

00:12:33.250 --> 00:12:35.480
<i>"The Dancing Girl" taught me 
how weak people can be.</i>

00:12:36.010 --> 00:12:38.480
<i>"Rashomon" taught me about the human ego.</i>

00:12:38.840 --> 00:12:41.290
<i>"The Moon Over the Mountain" 
taught me about pride.</i>

00:12:41.740 --> 00:12:44.980
<i>And </i>Kokoro<i> taught me 
about the human experience.</i>

00:12:46.240 --> 00:12:49.990
<i>In my mind, the world of fiction was reality,</i>

00:12:50.440 --> 00:12:53.340
<i>while the real world was a fabrication.</i>

00:12:53.340 --> 00:12:54.250
<i>That's why...</i>

00:12:55.090 --> 00:12:59.250
<i>meeting Ayai Yume was just 
as insignificant to me at first.</i>

00:12:59.770 --> 00:13:01.760
<i>I merely approached her on a whim.</i>

00:13:02.360 --> 00:13:05.260
<i>But when we went on our 
first date at the summer festival,</i>

00:13:05.580 --> 00:13:07.510
<i>something stirred deep within me.</i>

00:13:08.230 --> 00:13:10.900
<i>How could such a weak person exist?</i>

00:13:10.900 --> 00:13:13.720
<i>Someone so weak that she'd 
practically forget how to breathe</i>

00:13:13.720 --> 00:13:15.270
<i>if there were no one else around...</i>

00:13:15.990 --> 00:13:20.620
<i>If I abandoned her here, I thought
she'd be doomed to weep eternally</i>

00:13:20.620 --> 00:13:22.530
<i>in absolute solitude.</i>

00:13:22.920 --> 00:13:25.780
<i>"Oh, you poor thing..."</i>

00:13:26.790 --> 00:13:29.390
<i>That thought that arose within me</i>

00:13:29.390 --> 00:13:32.390
<i>was the exact sentiment 
others had thrown at me my whole life.</i>

00:13:33.340 --> 00:13:34.250
<i>Ayai...</i>

00:13:34.860 --> 00:13:37.180
<i>From that point on, 
you were etched into my heart.</i>

00:13:37.660 --> 00:13:40.140
<i>More intensely than any story I'd ever read.</i>

00:13:40.880 --> 00:13:42.400
<i>To me,</i>

00:13:42.400 --> 00:13:45.380
<i>you felt more real than anyone I'd ever met.</i>

00:13:47.830 --> 00:13:50.550
<i>Irido Mizuto has always struggled,</i>

00:13:50.550 --> 00:13:52.680
<i>forever keeping the world at arm's length.</i>

00:13:52.680 --> 00:13:53.560
<i>But then...</i>

00:13:54.230 --> 00:13:57.320
<i>One day, he stumbled
 upon his salvation, Ayai Yume.</i>

00:13:57.810 --> 00:14:02.940
<i>To him, she was the key to reversing 
his sentence of a pitiful life.</i>

00:14:04.140 --> 00:14:06.460
<i>But he lost that key.</i>

00:14:08.360 --> 00:14:10.920
<i>You shouldn't pity him
 for not having a mother.</i>

00:14:11.760 --> 00:14:15.280
<i>You should pity him because he lost 
the one thing that meant something to him.</i>

00:14:15.280 --> 00:14:16.330
<i>And that was...</i>

00:14:21.440 --> 00:14:23.710
You sure like dark and dingy places, huh?

00:14:25.140 --> 00:14:27.720
A wimp trying to turn over a new leaf, perhaps?

00:14:28.000 --> 00:14:30.520
Have you just come to ridicule me?

00:14:30.520 --> 00:14:33.970
To tell me I'm a loser who can't even 
interact with his own family?

00:14:33.970 --> 00:14:35.800
Don't be ridiculous.

00:14:35.800 --> 00:14:38.920
I figured that much out ages ago.

00:14:38.920 --> 00:14:40.940
It'd be pointless to dredge up.

00:14:42.200 --> 00:14:46.300
Remember our first date 
at the summer festival two years ago?

00:14:46.750 --> 00:14:50.820
I got lost and called you up in tears.

00:14:51.650 --> 00:14:52.450
Huh?

00:14:52.830 --> 00:14:55.260
I wonder how many days
 had passed after that...

00:14:55.260 --> 00:14:58.960
when you called me up 
out of the blue that one night.

00:14:59.780 --> 00:15:01.100
I remember it.

00:15:01.100 --> 00:15:04.710
I could hear the faint rustling 
of trees in the background.

00:15:05.200 --> 00:15:06.540
You were here, weren't you?

00:15:08.240 --> 00:15:09.740
You know...

00:15:09.740 --> 00:15:12.340
You must have really liked me, huh?

00:15:18.280 --> 00:15:19.660
Say, do you remember

00:15:20.110 --> 00:15:23.370
the date of when we shared our first kiss?

00:15:23.370 --> 00:15:26.230
October 27th, wasn't it?

00:15:26.860 --> 00:15:29.990
It was exactly two months 
after we had started dating.

00:15:30.380 --> 00:15:32.110
I knew you'd remember.

00:15:32.110 --> 00:15:33.490
And how's that?

00:15:33.490 --> 00:15:37.740
You were able to unlock my phone, were you not?

00:15:38.520 --> 00:15:42.000
You shouldn't be using a date 
as a password, you know.

00:15:42.000 --> 00:15:44.030
You say that...

00:15:44.030 --> 00:15:47.260
but the fact that your 
instinct was to type "1027"

00:15:47.260 --> 00:15:50.260
must mean you used it 
yourself at one point, no?

00:15:53.250 --> 00:15:55.890
That's right... 
We'd been dating exactly two months.

00:15:56.410 --> 00:16:00.650
I felt that if we didn't do it then, 
I'd have to wait a whole month to try again.

00:16:01.600 --> 00:16:03.140
So I was a little frantic at the time.

00:16:03.440 --> 00:16:08.780
I was sure you'd fallen for some dodgy 
advice you'd read online or in a magazine.

00:16:09.810 --> 00:16:14.280
I might have perused a few articles, 
but it was purely for research purposes.

00:16:14.280 --> 00:16:16.680
Either way, it's you we're talking about.

00:16:16.680 --> 00:16:18.840
There's no way you'd have
 done something so bold

00:16:18.840 --> 00:16:21.980
without reading about it first.

00:16:21.980 --> 00:16:24.890
Well, sorry for being so "by the book"!

00:16:24.890 --> 00:16:27.670
You could at least praise 
your girlfriend for being so courageous!

00:16:27.670 --> 00:16:29.340
You were very brave.

00:16:29.340 --> 00:16:31.800
You must have really practiced
 that kissing face too.

00:16:31.800 --> 00:16:33.550
How did you know?

00:16:33.550 --> 00:16:35.920
I knew the moment I saw it.

00:16:35.920 --> 00:16:39.310
There's no way you'd pull something
 like that off on your first try.

00:16:39.310 --> 00:16:40.700
You jerk!

00:16:40.700 --> 00:16:44.190
I'm pretty good at improv from time to time.

00:16:44.480 --> 00:16:48.190
Only because I'm usually the one
 backing you up after the fact.

00:16:48.190 --> 00:16:50.300
Oh, you're always so condescending.

00:16:50.300 --> 00:16:53.820
Don't you realize you'd be a better 
catch if you'd just bite your tongue?

00:16:53.820 --> 00:16:57.320
What reason do I have to try to adhere
 to your taste in men now?

00:16:57.610 --> 00:16:59.150
You're right.

00:16:59.150 --> 00:17:01.400
There'd be little point in it.

00:17:01.400 --> 00:17:03.580
It'd just end in disappointment
 for the both of us.

00:17:03.580 --> 00:17:06.580
You took the words right out of my mouth.

00:17:11.050 --> 00:17:11.840
Say...

00:17:12.550 --> 00:17:13.590
What?

00:17:14.030 --> 00:17:16.260
Why did you decide to go out with me?

00:17:17.160 --> 00:17:19.960
I probably would've been fine with anyone.

00:17:20.770 --> 00:17:21.850
What?!

00:17:22.250 --> 00:17:24.760
It was all just a twist of fate.

00:17:24.760 --> 00:17:26.300
A mere coincidence, wouldn't you say?

00:17:26.760 --> 00:17:30.620
Suppose I were to have met
 Higashira before I met you.

00:17:31.180 --> 00:17:33.860
In that case, we never would have dated.

00:17:35.240 --> 00:17:36.790
But the reality is...

00:17:37.480 --> 00:17:39.870
you're the one I met.

00:17:40.440 --> 00:17:44.500
In a simple game of musical chairs,
 whoever gets there first wins.

00:17:44.930 --> 00:17:48.020
If you're looking for a simple answer,
 that's the one I'd give.

00:17:50.230 --> 00:17:51.700
Are you satisfied?

00:17:52.440 --> 00:17:53.380
Yeah.

00:17:58.180 --> 00:17:59.740
It's almost time.

00:17:59.740 --> 00:18:00.390
Hmm?

00:18:00.900 --> 00:18:02.890
For the fireworks we never saw two years ago.

00:18:09.650 --> 00:18:12.650
We finally get to see them together.

00:18:28.150 --> 00:18:30.710
Hey... look at me.

00:18:38.880 --> 00:18:42.200
<i>Not as Ayai Yume, but as Irido Yume...</i>

00:18:42.640 --> 00:18:47.160
<i>I bestow unto you the second first kiss of my life.</i>

00:18:47.920 --> 00:18:50.260
<i>I assure you I will vanquish...</i>

00:18:50.850 --> 00:18:54.440
<i>the girl who's seized 
that one slot in your heart.</i>

00:18:55.910 --> 00:18:58.950
<i>No matter how much you may love Ayai Yume,</i>

00:19:07.450 --> 00:19:13.430
<i>I, Irido Yume, vow that I will 
win you over in the end.</i>

00:19:21.220 --> 00:19:25.280
Hey, tell me already! How'd yesterday go?

00:19:25.280 --> 00:19:28.360
I think we made a big step forward, at least.

00:19:28.730 --> 00:19:30.360
Let's go!

00:19:30.360 --> 00:19:32.940
If anything ever happens, call me, okay?!

00:19:32.940 --> 00:19:34.040
You have my full support—

00:19:34.040 --> 00:19:34.760
O-Ouch!

00:19:34.760 --> 00:19:36.410
Wh-What was that for, Chikuma?!

00:19:36.410 --> 00:19:37.820
Is this your rebellious phase?!

00:19:40.200 --> 00:19:41.280
Chikuma-kun?

00:19:43.450 --> 00:19:46.080
Wait, seriously? Is <i>that</i> what's going on?

00:19:47.580 --> 00:19:50.460
Um, how do I put this delicately?

00:19:50.460 --> 00:19:53.050
My condolences, I suppose.

00:19:55.670 --> 00:19:59.210
I can't thank you enough, Yume-chan.

00:19:59.210 --> 00:20:02.330
Take care of Mizuto for me, will you?

00:20:02.330 --> 00:20:04.430
He's very capable,

00:20:04.430 --> 00:20:06.720
so I'm sure he doesn't need my help.

00:20:07.040 --> 00:20:09.160
But it would be my pleasure.

00:20:09.160 --> 00:20:11.460
You wouldn't know it, 
but he gets quite lonely sometimes.

00:20:15.260 --> 00:20:17.400
What were you talking about with Granny?

00:20:17.710 --> 00:20:19.320
Take a wild guess.

00:20:20.580 --> 00:20:22.320
Why are you acting so weird?

00:20:22.810 --> 00:20:24.430
Don't worry about it.

00:20:24.430 --> 00:20:27.580
We're stepsiblings, after all, Mizuto-kun.

00:20:29.010 --> 00:20:31.580
Talk about stating the obvious, Yume-san.

00:20:39.460 --> 00:20:41.590
What is the meaning of this, Mizuto-kun?!

00:20:41.590 --> 00:20:43.840
Who is this flagrant playboy?!

00:20:44.160 --> 00:20:45.840
What the hell's going on, Irido?!

00:20:46.170 --> 00:20:48.100
Who's the chick with the massive jugs?!

00:20:48.950 --> 00:20:50.720
You stupid horndog.

00:20:51.050 --> 00:20:53.820
I'm your only friend, right, Mizuto-kun?!

00:20:53.820 --> 00:20:54.730
Right?!

00:20:54.730 --> 00:20:58.480
To think you'd go fooling around with this 
chick when you already have Irido-san...

00:20:58.920 --> 00:21:00.350
I'm disappointed in you.

00:21:00.350 --> 00:21:02.990
I thought you were better than that!

00:21:02.990 --> 00:21:06.650
Kawanami, this is Higashira Isana.

00:21:06.990 --> 00:21:09.990
She's just a friend I met recently
 and hit it off with.

00:21:10.300 --> 00:21:13.000
A friend you met recently and hit it off with?

00:21:13.340 --> 00:21:16.940
Higashira, this is Kawanami Kogure.

00:21:16.940 --> 00:21:21.250
He's just a classmate who declared himself 
my friend and insists on following me around.

00:21:21.720 --> 00:21:24.010
Someone who insists on following you around?

00:21:24.440 --> 00:21:25.510
Now I get it.

00:21:25.510 --> 00:21:28.010
He's your stalker, isn't he?

00:21:28.460 --> 00:21:29.510
Now I get it.

00:21:29.510 --> 00:21:31.640
She's a succubus who's chosen you as her prey.

00:21:31.640 --> 00:21:33.230
How did you arrive at <i>those</i> conclusions?

00:21:33.230 --> 00:21:36.410
Did you think he'd be an easy target
 just because he's a nerd?

00:21:36.410 --> 00:21:40.350
Well, too bad for you,
 but Irido isn't that shallow.

00:21:40.350 --> 00:21:43.400
Why don't you give up the charade
 before you take a hit to your pride?

00:21:43.400 --> 00:21:46.650
H-How could you so thoughtlessly 
prod at an open wound?!

00:21:46.650 --> 00:21:51.410
Oh dear, so you already got the rug
pulled out from under you, did you?

00:21:51.760 --> 00:21:53.560
Serves you right—

00:21:53.560 --> 00:21:56.030
Ow, ow, ow, ouch!

00:21:56.030 --> 00:21:59.200
There's nothing going on
 between her and Irido-kun, okay?

00:21:59.200 --> 00:22:01.580
They're just good friends.

00:22:01.580 --> 00:22:06.780
The fact that you suspect funny business
 is your sick little mind at work.

00:22:06.780 --> 00:22:07.800
You hear me?

00:22:07.800 --> 00:22:11.260
I'd rather not take lip from 
the chick with the sickest mind of all!

00:22:11.260 --> 00:22:12.180
What was that?

00:22:14.170 --> 00:22:17.660
Mizuto-kun and I just really click!

00:22:17.660 --> 00:22:20.360
It's because of love-obsessed 
wannabe players like you

00:22:20.360 --> 00:22:22.820
that I can't stand extroverts!

00:22:23.480 --> 00:22:28.000
You're not convincing anyone while
 glued to each other like that.

00:22:28.000 --> 00:22:29.570
Hands off for one second!

00:22:31.950 --> 00:22:36.410
I'm happy you finally made friends, 
unlike back in middle school,

00:22:36.410 --> 00:22:37.560
my dear little brother.

00:22:37.850 --> 00:22:41.470
And I'm thrilled you actually got 
something out of reinventing yourself,

00:22:41.470 --> 00:22:42.760
my dear little sister.

00:22:43.590 --> 00:22:45.590
<b>Irido</b>

00:22:46.260 --> 00:22:50.590
<i>Looking back, I can only describe 
it as youthful indiscretion.</i>

00:22:50.590 --> 00:22:58.350
<b>Saekano:
 How to Raise a
 Boring Girlfriend</b>

00:22:50.910 --> 00:22:54.990
<i>But from my second to third 
year of middle school,</i>

00:22:54.990 --> 00:22:57.960
<i>I had what you might call a girlfriend.</i>

00:22:58.730 --> 00:23:03.160
<i>But from my second to third 
year of middle school,</i>

00:23:03.160 --> 00:23:06.110
<i>I had what you might call a boyfriend.</i>

00:23:06.110 --> 00:23:09.990
The End Credits of The Fool
 Honobu Yonezawa

00:23:07.070 --> 00:23:09.990
<i>We can never go back to how things were.</i>

00:23:09.990 --> 00:23:13.740
Goodbye
Osamu Dazai

00:23:10.560 --> 00:23:13.740
<i>We can't bring back the happiness
 we felt back then.</i>

00:23:15.270 --> 00:23:16.260
<i>And yet...</i>

00:23:16.740 --> 00:23:21.250
<i>My feelings from that time
are still etched into my soul.</i>

00:23:22.610 --> 00:23:25.240
<i>For now, I'm okay with that.</i>

00:23:26.030 --> 00:23:28.840
<i>We still haven't fully moved on.</i>

00:23:29.700 --> 00:23:30.760
<i>But it's fine.</i>

00:23:30.760 --> 00:23:40.020
<b>Irido</b>

00:23:31.270 --> 00:23:34.440
<i>Because I... No, we...</i>

00:23:35.000 --> 00:23:38.010
<i>We have a chance to weave a new tale.</i>
